course: dictionary
lesson: 5764
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one is right. In «Mia puts two lumps of sugar in each cup», a lump is a small solid piece. In «Ben bumped his head and a lump came up», a lump is a swelling on the body.
explain: Ask yourself: what would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence. «Squeeze lemon into warm milk and it suddenly forms lumps» means small solid bits appear, because the milk's proteins clump together.
explain: Lump can also be a verb. To lump things together means to put them in one group. Phrases like «a lump in my throat» have their own meaning, so learn the whole phrase, not just the single word.
fact: Lump is a noun (lump, lumps) and a verb (lump together, lumps, lumped, lumping).
fact: A lump is a small solid piece of something with no clear shape, like a lump of sugar, clay or coal.
fact: A lump is also a swelling on the body, like a bump after you hit your head. Tell an adult if this happens.
fact: «A lump in my throat» means a tight feeling when you want to cry.
fact: «Lump together» means to put things in one group.
exercise: «Mia puts two lumps of sugar in each cup.» What is a lump here? | A group of people | A tight feeling in the throat | A swelling on the skin | *A small solid piece
exercise: «Ben bumped his head, and a lump came up.» What is a lump here? | A sweet taste | A cough | *A swelling on the body | A small solid piece of clay
exercise: Ravi wants to lump the red and green marbles together. What does lump together mean? | Throw them away | Paint them | *Put them in one group | Count them slowly
test: «Acid makes milk proteins clump into lumps.» What does lumps mean here? | Happy feelings | Loud noises | *Small solid pieces | Tall buildings
test: What does «a lump in my throat» mean? | *A tight feeling when you want to cry | A sweet taste | A cough that will not stop | A swelling you can see
exam: «A steel ship squashed into a lump would sink.» What does lump mean here? | *A solid piece with no clear shape | A small swelling | A sweet treat | To put things into a group
